e.</li>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":35,"text":" * <li>Executes each test method in its own transaction, which is automatically"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":36,"text":" * rolled back by default. This means that even if tests insert or otherwise"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":37,"text":" * change database state, there is no need for a teardown or cleanup script.</li>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":38,"text":" * <li>Provides useful inherited protected fields, such as a"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":39,"text":" * {@link SimpleJdbcTemplate} that can be used to verify database state after"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":40,"text":" * test operations, or verify the results of queries performed by application"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":41,"text":" * code. Alternatively, you can use protected convenience methods such as"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":42,"text":" * {@link #countRowsInTable(String)}, {@link #deleteFromTables(String[])},"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":43,"text":" * etc. An ApplicationContext is also inherited, and can be used for explicit"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":44,"text":" * lookup if necessary.</li>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":45,"text":" * </ul>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":46,"text":" * <p>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":47,"text":" * {@link AbstractJpaTests} and related classes are shipped in"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":48,"text":" * <code>spring-test.jar</code>."},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":49,"text":" * </p>"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":50,"text":" *"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":51,"text":" * @author Rod Johnson"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":52,"text":" * @author Sam Brannen"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":53,"text":" * @see AbstractJpaTests"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":54,"text":" */"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":55,"text":"public abstract class AbstractJpaClinicTests extends AbstractJpaTests {"},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":56,"text":""},{"type":"add","old":null,"new":57,"text